  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "In CompatibilityVersion 1, LEFT/RIGHT preserve astral pairs, MID slices UTF-16 units, and 32,767-unit overflow errors differ by function",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (CompatibilityVersion 1), LEFT and RIGHT preserve valid UTF-16 surrogate pairs when counting characters (LEFT(UNICHAR(128512),1) returns '😀', whose LEN is 2), whereas MID slices raw UTF-16 code units and can emit an unpaired surrogate (MID(UNICHAR(128512),1,1) returns 0xd83d). Exceeding the 32,767 UTF-16 code-unit cell limit gives #VALUE! in REPT, SUBSTITUTE, and REPLACE, #CALC! in CONCAT, and silent truncation to 32,767 units in CONCATENATE and TEXTJOIN (which can leave an unpaired high surrogate when an astral character straddles index 32,767).",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across all 76 rows of dcfl2_text in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 under CompatibilityVersion 1.",
